          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP269 Twin Lakes

N 51° 12.545 W 113° 49.115&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Well, that was interesting.  This is my last cap for the day.  I tried to approach this cache from the north (the only way possible as far as I know) but driving on this road was restricted so I had to walk the last ~325m to GZ.  I'm not sure why though because the road (at least up till GZ) seemed to be fine.  Secondly, I'm a bit confused by the name of this BC as I didn't see any water nearby.  Did I miss it/them?  At least, GZ was well marked and the cap was easily visible.  According to the hint, I may be missing something else too.  Hopefully I found what I was supposed to.  TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
